    "submission": "submission-transconf.json",
    "summary": "Turn 83 turned the last recorded map discrepancy into a check: the executor's documented transitive-conflict skipping is inert.\n\nThe discrepancy. The implementation's own header lists transitive-conflict skipping among its differences from the original code base — skipping the wait for prior commands that commute with the instance being executed — and the executor contains a branch gated on the transconf flag that walks every command pair and takes no action when nothing conflicts. A caller can enable the flag through the constructor, yet the branch changes nothing.\n\nObservation. The new harness builds exactly the documented situation with the flag on: a committed instance whose command touches one key and whose only dependency is an uncommitted command on a different key, with the two commands verified to commute under the state package's relation. The local construction run reports commands_commute true, the dependency still PREACCEPTED and executed false — execution halts on that dependency exactly as if the flag were off, leaving the row stopped.\n\nObligation and check (new claim C12-transitive-skip-executes-commuting-command, implementation semantics, priority 1). With transitive-conflict skipping enabled, executing an instance must not wait for a prior command it commutes with. The check asserts executed == true on the execution event with the flag and the commuting pair as prerequisite conditions, a binding on the closure computation that contains the branch, and grounding in the documented feature plus the branch's empty body; the claim is bounded to callers that enable the flag (the launcher passes false, cited from the epaxos.New call site after correcting the range) and its consequence is performance rather than safety, which the rationale states along with the open question of whether the intended pruning was to drop the dependency or to relax the ready check.\n\nFrontier. Twelve claim families are now in flight or settled; this is the last discrepancy recorded in the map that had not been checked, and it joins the others with the reader-side codec reaction still the single item that cannot be exercised in-package. No requirement, premise or earlier observation was weakened."
